  <event id="159">
      <start>15:00</start>
      <duration>01:00</duration>
      <room>AW1.120</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Workflow In Java</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>JBoss</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://labs.jboss.com/jbossjbpm/&#34;&gt;JBoss jBPM&lt;/a&gt; is an open source platform that supports workflow, business process management, and service orchestration.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Though BPEL has a big brand name associated to BPM, people start to realize that it is not a silver bullet. Recently two process component models have taken a different point of view. Multiple process languages are taken as the goal and process component models are frameworks on which multiple languages can be build.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We&amp;#39;ll look at some examples of the Process Virtual Machine and explain how this technology can be used as the basis for workflow, BPM and orchestration.  Attending this talk will give a good overview of the complete &lt;a href=&#34;http://labs.jboss.com/jbossjbpm/&#34;&gt;JBoss jBPM project&lt;/a&gt;.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="1591">Tom Baeyens</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>